body: "pm-cli CI runs package extension commands through node dist/cli.js and does not install a global pm binary. pm-changelog's extension handler called readPmItems with the default pm binary, so changelog generate failed in CI with extension_command_handler_failed after command activation succeeded.\\n\\nFix: the extension now falls back to the current Node CLI entrypoint when the default pm binary is unavailable, and adds a regression test that invokes node @unbrained/pm-cli/dist/cli.js with PATH limited to the Node binary directory.\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (1)\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-05-23T21:20:50Z)\n>\n> Fixed in main at f5ebc23. The extension command now reads tracker items through the active pm SDK path and passes the Node CLI/no-global-pm regression under GITHUB_ACTIONS=true; GitHub Actions run 26343824903 is green. Npm publication of 2026.5.23-5 is blocked by npm 2FA/bypass-token requirements, so downstream pm-cli is pinned to the verified GitHub source until publish is authorized."
